 "interpretations": [
  "Cell set: the stats use every cell present. The pre-registered matrix is Runner 4 (t in {1, 16} x alone / batched) and llama.cpp 16 (x fa x ub); the t=1 cells run after the release (ruled), so until then K counts identity across the t=16 cells only (Runner 2, llama.cpp 8, Unsloth 8), factors that need t=1 are 'pending', and the 2.4 wording's 'all 4 settings' / '16 settings' text would overstate the measured cells. RULED (CLAIM2-INTERPRETATIONS-2026-11-26-stats.md 1): the 2.4 wordings are NOT used until the t=1 cells run; before then the figures are 'the sixteen-thread half, provisional, t=1 pending', and the branch the t=16 counts point to is shown as provisional only.",
  "Byte identity: 'the raw generated UTF-8 byte string (and generated token ID sequence up to EOS or 256 tokens)' is read as the target request's gen_ids AND the bytes decode(gen_ids) gives with the file's vocabulary (byte-level tokens through the inverse bytes_to_unicode, special tokens as their text). Equal ids give equal bytes, so the bytes add nothing but are checked. Runner's gen_ids carry the client-appended 200006 on stopped turns (stop_token_appended; its receipt lacks it); this is the same in every Runner cell, so identity is unaffected.",
  "Records: the last COMPLETE line per target id (the client's resume rule); incomplete or torn lines are counted and reported. Per cell: 20 targets; prompt_ids equal across all of an engine's cells (checked).",
  "Throughput: agg_tok_s per batched round = sum over its 9 requests of len(gen_ids) / T_batch_wall_s (barrier release to the 9th response, the client's T_batch_wall_s = the last end_offset_s); alone tok/s per round = len(gen_ids) / T_batch_wall_s of its one request (prefill included, as the wall is). len(gen_ids) is the generated id count (Claim 3's ruled interpretation 7); the client's agg_tok_s (usage counts) is shown beside where it differs (Runner's appended stop token). Median and IQR by claim1_stats.quartiles_iqr. The quoted R_* / L_* / U_* cells are the builds' resolved defaults (fa on, ub 512; the supervisor's ruling and the defaults probes); Runner has no fa / ub. Each figure carries its load-table row (median / peak load1, resident min, share of samples with resident < 0.99) and the ruled sentence on Runner's page loss.",
  "llama.cpp co-batching (CB_L): /metrics was off (PREREG 1.2's flag line has no --metrics: status 501) and the per-decode batch lines are below the server's default verbosity, so 'active sequences per decode batch' is not logged. Read instead: every generating slot's token enters ONE shared batch per update_slots iteration (tools/server/server-context.cpp:3726, batch.add at :4430 / :4562), and llama_decode splits it into micro-batches of n_ubatch (src/llama-context.cpp:2254). So CB = true for a cell when >= 2 slots generated at once AND n_ubatch > 1; with -ub 1 each micro-batch holds one token, i.e. the sequences decode one at a time inside one call (CB = false at the kernel level). Concurrency = slots between 'launch_slot_' and 'release' in the server's stderr: time-weighted mean while >= 1 is active, max, and the share of that time with >= 2. RULED (5): stated as 'inferred from the source and the slot log'.",
  "Runner co-batching: co_batched = false is PREREG 2's architectural statement (MANUAL.md:2685; sequential MoE decode). Its evidence: /metrics runner_batch_steps_total and runner_batch_sequences_total per round (after - before; mean sequences per step = the scheduler's slot count per step, not shared matmuls). The RUNNER_DEBUG_ROUTE=1 'path=' lines PREREG names CANNOT appear for this model at 7bf8b64d: model_forward_batch returns through model_inkling2_forward before route_ran() (src/model.c:17497); the env was set (run_claim2_t16.sh:75). Disclosed, not a run problem (risk-note 12). RULED (6), with a source check, CONFIRMED at 7bf8b64d: the server's one decode thread calls model_batch_decode once per step over the gathered slots (src/scheduler.c:197-214) and counts steps += 1, sequences += nb (:222-223), so the counters' mean is the slots GATHERED per step; with no device (--gpu off: model.c:6511, the load log's '0 layers'; no backend: gpu_none.c:448-451) model_batch_decode skips gpu_batch_decode (model.c:18197-18199) and runs the sequential fallback, model_forward per sequence in turn (:18271-18275), each a one-row forward (:18112-18114, n = 1) through model_inkling2_forward (:17497). One sequence at a time; no multi-sequence matrix product.",
  "Factor attribution (2.3 2): each count is the number of the 20 targets whose output differs between the reference cell (alone, t=16, fa on, ub 512; Runner: alone, t=16) and the cell that changes ONLY that factor: alone vs batched at t=16 (and at t=1, from the t=1 alone cell), t=16 vs t=1 alone and batched, fa on vs off, ub 512 vs 1. The 2.4 branch 3 '<failing factor>' lists Runner's factors with a non-zero count.",
  "Companions (information, not a PREREG metric): each of the 8 fixed companions runs once per batched round, 20 times per batched cell; reported: distinct outputs per companion within each cell, and whether its output is the same across all of the engine's batched cells.",
  "Unsloth's column (ADDENDUM-2026-11-24-unsloth.md, 'an additional column in the same tables'): K_U / 20 with its Wilson interval, factor counts, CB_U, U_batched / U_alone, the companions. PREREG 0.2 defines paired comparisons for Claims 1 and 3 only and Claim 2 has no outcome rule between engines, so there is no Claim 2 'pair' to compute and no combined label (as ruled for Claim 3). The 2.4 outcome and wording use Runner and mainline only. RULED (9): confirmed, no pairs."
 ],
